    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123-a5">

                <pb facs="0308" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg236"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 349.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Tinsly</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 24,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have your letter of the 22d. It must be
                    distinctly understood that this money is not offered to the prisoners to induce
                    them to leave Ireland.</p>
                <p>It is to be given them simply as an act of kindness to enable them, in case of
                    their release without funds, to return to America.</p>
                <p>I inclose the form of a receipt which you desire.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp; c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
